WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.450
In 2025, UK residents made an
estimated 99.9 million visits abroad.

2
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:11.470
Indian nationals made 32.8
million departures abroad,

3
00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.590
22 per cent more than in 2019.

4
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:19.150
Yet India has about 21 times
as many people as the UK.

5
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.270
Is it simply a matter of taste?

6
00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.150
Are there too few airports?

7
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.730
So why the gap?

8
00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:28.490
In this mission, you'll define
leisure, tourism and sport,

9
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:32.290
and sort trips by cost,
duration and destination.

10
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:34.990
Then you'll compare
three societies: China,

11
00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.670
with more than 6.5 billion
domestic trips in 2025,

12
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.750
India and the UK.

13
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:46.390
Your mission: explain why the UK makes
far more trips abroad than India,

14
00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.270
with far fewer people.
